SOAPBOX: As usual, spent more time in the chair than I expected to. That seems to happen when Doug AB8M and I are neck and neck on the online scoreboard..
SOAPBOX: The first half of this contest is just awful. 20 meters is a slog, with lots of QRM and QSB which makes it difficult to get any consistent rate going, at least with 100w and a wire. Once the sun goes down and 40/80 jump to life, it's an entirely different ballgame.
SOAPBOX: Crashed at about 0600z and got back up for the last two hours, which were awesome.
SOAPBOX: If the second half of this thing wasn't so much fun, I probably woulnd't do it again.
SOAPBOX: 73 de KM8V
